.TH FERROR 3S  "August 1, 1992"
.ds ]W ANSI C
.SH NAME
ferror, feof, clearerr, fileno \- stream status inquiries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int feof(FILE *\fIstream\fP);
.PP
.B int ferror(FILE *\fIstream\fP);
.PP
.B void clearerr(FILE *\fIstream\fP);
.PP
.B int fileno(FILE *\fIstream\fP);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Feof
returns non-zero when end of file is read on the named input
.IR stream ,
otherwise zero.
Unless cleared by
.IR clearerr ,
the end-of-file indication lasts until
the stream is closed.
.PP
.I Ferror
returns non-zero when an error has occurred reading or writing
the named
.IR stream ,
otherwise zero.
Unless cleared by
.IR clearerr ,
the error indication lasts until
the stream is closed.
.PP
.I Clearerr
resets the error and end-of-file indicators on the named
.IR stream .
.PP
.I Fileno
(which is not an ANSI C function)
returns the integer file descriptor
associated with the
.IR stream ,
see
.IR open (2).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
open(2),
fopen(3S)
